The '''Hersatia national football team''' represents [[Hersatia]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Hersatia Football Federation]] and is one of the better-known western Illypnian sides with a long domestic tradition and a compact, technically oriented playing style. Hersatia opened their [[2026 AFA World Cup|2026 World Cup]] campaign with a stoppage-time 1–0 win over [[Ayorin national football team|Ayorin]].

== History ==

=== Early development ===
Hersatian football developed around the major cities of the kingdom's western and central river valleys, with clubs in Gravere, Onsernon, Prespiêrs, and Troevey forming the core of the domestic game. The national team became associated with a cultured, tactically flexible style that reflected the country's broader traditions of courtly organisation and civic rivalry.

=== Modern era ===
In the modern era, Hersatia have built a reputation as a stubborn and difficult opponent, particularly in qualifiers and regional tournaments. Their 2026 World Cup debut has been greeted as an important step for the country's football program, and the opening-day victory over Ayorin immediately raised expectations that the team could progress beyond the group stage.

== Stadium ==

Hersatia play their home matches at [[Gravere National Stadium]] in [[Gravere]], the kingdom's principal football venue. Important matches are also occasionally staged in [[Onsernon]], [[Prespiêrs]], and [[Troevey]].

== Playing style ==

Hersatia are generally described as a technically composed side that favours measured build-up play, narrow passing combinations, and disciplined positional structure. The team is usually at its best when it can control the tempo and force opponents into longer possessions without the ball.

